Case I: $P(-4, 3)$ divides the segment $AB$
internally in the ratio $5:3$. By the section formula $-4 = \frac{5(0) + 3(a)}{5 + 3}
\implies -4 = \frac{3a}{8} \implies a = -\frac{32}{3}$ and $3 = \frac{5(b) + 3(0)}{5 + 3}
\implies 3 = \frac{5b}{8} \implies b = \frac{24}{5}$.

Case II: $P(-4, 3)$ divides the segment $BA$
internally in the ratio $5:3$. By the section formula $-4 = \frac{5(a) + 3(0)}{5 + 3}
\implies -4 = \frac{5a}{8} \implies a = -\frac{32}{5}$ and $3 = \frac{5(0) + 3(b)}{5 + 3}
\implies 3 = \frac{3b}{8} \implies b = 8$.

Using the angle between two lines formula: $\tan 45^\circ = \left| \frac{m - m_0}{1 + m m_0}
\right| \implies 1 = \left| \frac{m - \left(-\frac{2}{3}\right)}{1 + m\left(-\frac{2}{3}\right)}
\right| = \left| \frac{3m + 2}{3 - 2m} \right|$

The area of $\triangle ABG$ is given by $\text{Area of }(\triangle ABG) = \frac{1}{2}
\cdot |AG| \cdot |BG| = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(\frac{2}{3}m\right) \cdot \left(\frac{2}{3}n\right)
= \frac{2}{9}mn$.

The area of $\triangle BGD$ is given by $\text{Area of }(\triangle BGD) = \frac{1}{2}
\cdot |GD| \cdot |BG| = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \left(\frac{1}{3}m\right) \cdot \left(\frac{2}{3}n\right)
= \frac{1}{9}mn$.
